layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiTherefore as the church is subject unto Christ, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYHusbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLthat he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–that he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]So ought men to love their wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife loveth himself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgFor no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as the Lord the church:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?for we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined unto his wife, and they two shall be one flesh.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFThis is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Christ and the church.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒNevertheless, let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself; and the wife see that she reverence her husband.¦layout ªlast_verse!